// corpus: known-failure string operators reject a `character` argument (ROADMAP: "String operators reject a `character`")
// Acronym: first letter of each word, upper-cased. Hyphens separate words.
// `w[1]` is a character; `toUpperCase` declares `(string) -> string` and
// refuses it, so this natural spelling is a static type error today.
acronym(s) = stringJoin(map(w => toUpperCase(w[1]), stringSplit(stringReplace(s, "-", " "))), "")
(acronym("Portable Network Graphics"), acronym("Complementary metal-oxide semiconductor"), acronym("Ruby on Rails"))
// ➔ ("PNG", "CMOS", "ROR")
